## Monthly Mean Temperature   

### 30-year normals  

Based on monthly averages over a 30-year period (1991-2020; see @tbl-tempMonthly30yr and @fig-tempMonthly30yr), the coldest month in the Mississippi Sound Watershed is January. The lowest mean January value, in the northern part of the watershed, is 43.5 °F, with temperatures along the coast being higher at 52 °F. The hottest month is July, at 79.8 °F in the northern part of the watershed and 82.7 °F along the coast.


